Z||000000||Rodney||12-09-2001||08:00 PM||||I have the adjustable clutch banjos on my web page now. I had wondered if they were a worthy item. I seem to see a lot with clutches not fully releasing and bent clutch pedals that I felt maybe they would be useful. So I have decided to offer them. Certainly not a cure all for clutch release problems but maybe useful to a certain degree. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/n90.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/n90.html</A>    Adjustable clutch banjo<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||12-09-2001||09:54 PM||||My check is in the mail.<P>No, really . . . .<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||recluse||12-09-2001||10:23 PM||||Rodney,  I ordered one of these and I was going to instal it yesterday.  I got the washer off of and the opening in the washer is too large, or the flared out tip on the end of the pushrod is too small, the washer slid right though.  It was an extra one I had, and I think it came off of my 86 GT parts car but i dont think theres a difference.  This is for my 87 GT.  Just though I would let you know.  But besides that it seems very high quality, now where to find a washer that will work?  ||||reg||4
Z||000003||Rodney||12-10-2001||08:54 AM||||Since I only have 2 used banjos here I am guessing there are some variations on the retaining washer. I know the head of mine is slightly smaller and it did concern me. I can get a special cocave hardened steel thin washer that should fix it. Send me an address and I'll send you one. ||||reg||1
